set.body:
Add executable support for the completed nonsmooth and coordinate-constraint vocabulary.

Families:
- L1, feature-row L21, disjoint and overlapping groups, sparse-group, elastic net;
- nonnegative, box, simplex, and monotone constraints;
- total variation and aligned-score penalties through composite lowering.

Guarantees must reflect the compiled problem: global convex only when proved, otherwise stationary, coordinatewise-stationary, or feasible-point evidence.

Acceptance:
- independent small convex oracles, KKT residuals, and primal-dual gaps;
- overlapping groups always use the exact lifted-variable formulation;
- unsupported PSD, Stiefel, fixed-support, or rank combinations fail during compilation;
- chart laws, symmetry, gauge, and result equivalence survive lowering;
- numerical stopping and infeasibility are typed and inspectable;
- JVM and Scala.js pass.
